# Grouped GEMM shapes
# Format: --grouped=<dim_idx>:<num_groups>:<sizes|profile> MxK:GxKxN
# Where:
#   dim_idx      - dimension index to group (0=M, 1=K)
#   num_groups   - number of groups/experts
#   sizes        - a named profile (balanced/hot/decode) synthesized from the
#                  shape's M. '+'-separated explicit lists are also accepted but
#                  intentionally unused here - every case is profile-generated.
#   M            - total M dimension size
#   G            - number of groups/experts (must match num_groups above)
#
# Note: --reset after batching this file to avoid leaking --grouped

# Uniform
--grouped=0:4:balanced
32x64:4x64x32
--grouped=0:8:balanced
64x64:8x64x64
--grouped=0:16:balanced
32x128:16x128x96

# Unbalanced (one dominant expert)
--grouped=0:3:hot
16x32:3x32x24
--grouped=0:4:hot
100x64:4x64x32
--grouped=0:5:hot
31x64:5x64x32

# Single group (E=1: the whole M is one group)
--grouped=0:1:balanced
8x16:1x16x12
# Empty + varied mix (hot draw at M=E leaves some groups empty: [3,1,1,1,0,0])
--grouped=0:6:hot
6x24:6x24x20

# Sparse groups: decode (many empty, size-1) + one-expert-absorbs-all (hot:100).
--grouped=0:32:decode,0:32:hot:100
4x128:32x128x64

--grouped=0:256:balanced,0:256:hot:100
255x128:256x128x64
